# Build output.
/target

# rustfmt backups, left behind when `--backup` is used.
**/*.rs.bk

# Byte-code from the Python CI policy scripts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# macOS Finder metadata. Committing it once is enough to annoy every other host.
.DS_Store

# Machine-local planning and design inputs are managed outside the product repository.
# Listed explicitly rather than relying on the machine-global excludes file, so a
# contributor who does not have that file cannot commit them here by accident.
/rasen/
/.rasen/

# A convenience checkout of the frozen `master` branch, used as the behavioural
# reference during the rewrite. Machine-local; the branch itself is the real reference.
/examples/

# Real archives used to exercise the tool by hand. Machine-local, not test data and not
# evidence: they are someone's library, so they must never be committed.
/samples/

# Third-party tools fetched to build fixtures this project cannot write itself. `rar` is
# RARLAB's proprietary archiver, and it is the only program that can create a RAR archive:
# UnRAR's licence forbids using its source to re-create the compression algorithm, so no
# open implementation exists or can. Machine-local, never committed, and never used by CI.
# `tests/fixtures/make-rar-fixtures.sh` fetches it and says why.
/tools/

# The machine-global excludes file ignores `AGENTS.md` so that agent scratch files stay
# out of unrelated repositories. Here it is a tracked symbolic link to `CLAUDE.md` and
# is part of the repository, so that rule is cancelled.
!/AGENTS.md
